    "description": "A mobile sync engine on iOS fetches four kinds of payload (contacts, calendar, documents, settings) concurrently and merges them into one local state. The current implementation launches detached tasks per payload, keeps a mutable dictionary across them with a lock, and leaks two tasks on every logout because nothing waits for them; cancellation after a network drop occasionally leaves half-merged state and a background refresh that keeps running into the next session. The team wants a parent work unit that owns its children: if one fails or the user cancels, every child is cancelled and awaited before the merge is abandoned, and the engine reports one outcome to the caller. The decision to implement: how concurrent child tasks are spawned, awaited and cancelled under one parent scope so lifetimes are bounded and cleanup is deterministic.",
    "decision_statement": "Spawn, await and cancel concurrent child tasks under one parent scope with deterministic cleanup.",
    "notes": "Holdout family: fork-join/future-promise stay acceptable for the older API-shaped solutions."
  },
